From 6d283b97adb609236d91b822687eb206f17d13b7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Refactor Bot <refactor@local>
Date: Tue, 25 Aug 2026 06:05:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/9] fix(i18n,nav): translate navigation and stop dropping the
 locale on links

- Header/Footer labels were hardcoded English on an otherwise 4-locale site.
  Moved them to new Nav/Footer message namespaces (en/fa/az/tr).
- Header menu linked to /projects (no such route -> 404) and omitted
  /industries (which exists). Menu now points at real routes:
  Home, About, Services, Industries, Contact.
- Footer, Hero CTA, the cookie-banner privacy link and the projects carousel
  used next/link directly, which drops the /[locale] prefix and breaks
  language routing. Switched them to the locale-aware Link from i18n/navigation.
- Projects carousel cards linked to non-existent /projects/* detail pages.
  href is now optional and cards render as non-links until those routes exist.
- Active-nav detection now matches nested routes (startsWith), not just exact.
